timekeeping: export timekeeping_inject_sleeptime64

The emulator's standby is suspend-to-idle with the VM stopped by the host, as a TV powers its SoC
down. CLOCK_MONOTONIC must leave that time out (kvm-adjvtime and kvm-clock do), and
CLOCK_REALTIME and CLOCK_BOOTTIME must include it, as on a TV. The stock rtc_resume skips the
injection under s2idle without a cpuidle driver (timekeeping_rtc_skipresume: timekeeping_suspend
never ran), so lgemu.ko reads the RTC across the suspend and injects the difference itself
(guest/kernel/modules/lgemu/i2c.c, "the SoC powered down"), the same way rtc_resume does.

--- a/kernel/time/timekeeping.c
+++ b/kernel/time/timekeeping.c
@@ -1930,6 +1930,7 @@
 	/* Signal hrtimers about time change */
 	clock_was_set(CLOCK_SET_WALL | CLOCK_SET_BOOT);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(timekeeping_inject_sleeptime64);
 #endif
 
